{"organizations": [], "uuid": "da4bae71cf21d9300b03c9c924af912564cb70bd", "thread": {"social": {"gplus": {"shares": 0}, "pinterest": {"shares": 0}, "vk": {"shares": 0}, "linkedin": {"shares": 0}, "facebook": {"likes": 0, "shares": 0, "comments": 0}, "stumbledupon": {"shares": 0}}, "site_full": "www.msn.com", "main_image": "", "site_section": "http://www.msn.com/en-us/money", "section_title": "Stock quotes, financial tools, news and analysis - MSN Money", "url": "http://www.msn.com/en-us/money/companies/in-n-out-managers-make-dollar160000-a-year-reports-show/ar-AAvaT7u", "country": "US", "domain_rank": 13, "title": "In-N-Out managers make $160,000 a year, reports show", "performance_score": 0, "site": "msn.com", "participants_count": 1, "title_full": "", "spam_score": 0.0, "site_type": "news", "published": "2018-01-25T02:00:00.000+02:00", "replies_count": 0, "uuid": "da4bae71cf21d9300b03c9c924af912564cb70bd"}, "author": "Josh Hafner", "url": "http://www.msn.com/en-us/money/companies/in-n-out-managers-make-dollar160000-a-year-reports-show/ar-AAvaT7u", "ord_in_thread": 0, "title": "In-N-Out managers make $160,000 a year, reports show", "locations": [], "entities": {"persons": [{"name": "josh hafner", "sentiment": "negative"}, {"name": "saru jayaraman", "sentiment": "none"}], "locations": [{"name": "usa", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "bay area", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "irvine", "sentiment": "none"}], "organizations": [{"name": "apple inc", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "intel corp", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "california sun", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "cbs los angeles", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "starbucks corp", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "cbs los angeles video", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "amazon.com inc", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "ktvu", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "uc berkley's food research center", "sentiment": "none"}]}, "highlightText": "", "language": "english", "persons": [], "text": "In-N-Out managers make $160,000 a year, reports show USA TODAY 5 hrs ago Josh Hafner In-N-Out: What A Hamburger And A 6-Figure Salary Are All About CBS Los Angeles Video by CBS Los Angeles\nWhen you think of six-figure salaries, flipping burgers may not come to mind. But In-N-Out, the cult favorite fast food chain, sees its store managers earning over $160,000 on average, the company told the California Sun .\nPopular Searches Starbucks Corp SBUX\n▼ 60.55 -0.28 -0.46% Intel Corp INTC\n▼ 45.30 -0.21 -0.46% Apple Inc AAPL\n▼ 171.11 -3.11 -1.79% Amazon.com Inc AMZN\n▲ 1,377.95 +20.44 +1.51% “In-N-Out is just eons above everybody else,” Saru Jayaraman, director of UC Berkley's Food Research Center, told the newsletter. “On wages and benefits, they really are the best large chain.”\nThe Irvine, Calif.-based company confirmed the eye-popping figure to the Bay Area's KTVU news , noting that managers oversee only one location each. They ultimately become responsible for all aspects of the restaurant, from employee training to the cleanliness of counter tops.\nIn-N-Out workers can start at $13 an hour (minimum wage is $11 for California's larger companies), KTVU reported, and work their way up to that $160,000-ish salary without a college degree.\nThe gig's no cake walk, though: A top review of In-N-Out from an employee on Glassdoor , a jobs listing site, notes a \"fast-paced environment\" with \"very hard\" work and \"no shortcuts.\"\nIn-N-Out Vice President of Operations Denny Warnick told the Sun that quality service requires quality employees with quality pay — a vision of the company's founders, Harry and Esther Snyder.\n“Paying their associates well was just one way to help maintain that focus, and those beliefs remain firmly in place with us today,” Warnick told the Sun.\nSee the full report at the California Sun.\nGo to MSN Home", "external_links": ["http://prod-video-cms-amp-microsoft-com.akamaized.net/tenant/amp/entityid/AAv8H3e?blobrefkey=en-us&$blob=1&quot;,&quot;culture&quot;:&quot;en-us&quot;}